  "problem": "Clients could guess after source/generation limits. A cursor for one tool/query could page a different collection. An expired cursor could silently begin a new generation. An unknown schema could be treated as an empty list of variables. HTTP 200 could be treated as task completion. Nonretryable states could be retried. Cancellation might not stop the current request. Next-cursor and omitted-section explanations could be lost.",
  "resulting_behavior": "A cursor for one tool/query cannot page a different collection. An expired cursor never silently begins a new generation. Restart instructions preserve the research question and disclose snapshot change. An unknown schema is not returned as an empty list of variables or a transport success claiming the task completed. Cancellation stops the current request. Clients neither retry nonretryable states nor lose the next-cursor/omitted-section explanation. Recovery behavior is documented with runnable examples. No acceptance check depends solely on status 200. A successful tool envelope is not a completed research task. worker/index.mjs does not import enrichment. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
